johnwalbright@aol.com (JohnWAlbright) writes:

> Food Poisoning

Fresh food only.  Directly after the kill they're best.
Watch your pet, it knows quite well what you may eat 
safely.  You can eat lichens, btw, despite your cats/dogs 
lack of interest in them.  They're vegetarian.  

> Gnomish Mines (great place to get some good equipment but usually too tough)

So don't go there until you feel ready.  At the beginning, I 
always went down there first.  Now I complete Sokoban first, and 
consider if I'm ready afterwards.  My guys live longer this way.  

> Wererats (lycanthropy stinks)

Let your pet deal with them.  Do you know the E-word trick?  
Anyway, spend some time in the upper levels until your pet 
looks strong enough to deal with such werefoos.  Btw, 
lycantrophy ain't all bad.  You can summon weak but 
abound 'pets' (cool if you know of a polymorph trap 
somewhere, e.g.).  You just try to get the best out of 
your situation.  Your god can free you from this curse, 
if he's feeling that way.

> running out of food

Usually, your prayer timeout is much shorter than the 
time between normale and 'fainting' status.  At the beginning, 
it's not the worst strategy to pray for food (nice t-shirt motto, 
btw:  "Will pray for food.").  You should even continue to pray 
for food if you found one or two food rations, and save them 
for a time your god is not pleased.  

> generally running into monster that kick my butt and ruin all my fun.

Run, run, run.  You must choose the place and time to fight 
to maximize your chances.  Fight in narrow corridors.  Behind 
corners.  Train your pet (let him kill a lot of low-level monsters), 
try to get low AC by all means, try to keep lower level until you 
have lower AC, try a little alchemy to improve your HPs, use the 
E-word and soften larger monsters by firing all you have at them.  
Don't, don't, don't be close-fisted with your goodies.  If 
you're dead, they won't help you anyway.  My last char died 
with two wands of death in the gnomish mines just because I 
didn't want to _waste_ them.  (Dumb, dumb, dumb!)  
And don't get burdened, not even for a crystal plate mail 
(train your strength by pushing boulders, and your Const by 
eating monsters helps improving your maxweight.)

[classes played so far]
> Rogue
> Barbarian
> Samarai
> Priest
> Wizard

Try healers.  They're really good for learning some basic 
facts.  Take your time and make frequent use of your stethoscope, 
it can teach you some things which are more fun learning 
by yourself than reading in a spoiler.  Plus, they have 
healing spells, which helps a lot, in particular for your 
pets.  

